# The mouse wheel scrolls the Settings list — the box is 35 rows tall for
# a long list. A notch down moves the top of the list away; the cursor
# follows the window (the row it marks is always visible), and a notch
# up brings the top back.
command view.settings
expect screen contains "── UI ──"
scroll 60 20 down
expect screen lacks "── UI ──"
scroll 60 20 up
expect screen contains "── UI ──"
# A row per notch (Rust's `settings_move_row(±1)` an event): forty
# notches carry the 43-row UI section past and the Editor header in,
# at the box's height on any screen the suite runs at.
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
